# What gets uploaded is frontend/ and nothing else.
#
# Without this the CLI uploads data/ as well — 12 GB across 7,333 files — and
# the deploy dies during upload with an empty "Unexpected error ()".
#
# `npm run build` fills frontend/api/ with the JSON the site reads. Everything
# that produced it stays on this machine, package.json included: with no
# package.json up there, Vercel has no build script to find and runs none. The
# site is already built.
#
# Note this file REPLACES .gitignore for deploys rather than adding to it, so
# node_modules has to be named here too.
#
# Every pattern is anchored with a leading slash. Without it these match at any
# depth — a bare `xg` also excludes frontend/api/xg/, which silently ships a
# site whose every match 404s while the upload still "succeeds" at 541 KB.

/data
/node_modules
/xg
/tools
/server.js
/package.json
/package-lock.json
/README.md
/CLAUDE.md
/.claude
/.git
/.env*
